\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of MATE-CLIP. The frozen CLIP backbone is shared by the text and video encoders. On the text side, a static semantic branch (frozen semantic bank) is combined with a learnable branch enhanced by AMTF (multi-strategy text fusion over the \texttt  {[EOT]}, masked-mean, and masked-attention views), and the two branches are fused adaptively into action-biased prototypes. On the video side, MGTA selects discriminative spatial-temporal regions and performs dual-branch temporal modeling (dense Conv3d + sparse asynchronous attention); a lightweight frame-aggregation mixer (Mixer) then applies a depthwise temporal convolution to the frame features before the temporal mean. Finally, BFEM bidirectionally enhances the video feature and the text prototypes with each other under zero-initialized gates. The CLIP backbone remains frozen throughout.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{4}{Overview of MATE-CLIP. The frozen CLIP backbone is shared by the text and video encoders. On the text side, a static semantic branch (frozen semantic bank) is combined with a learnable branch enhanced by AMTF (multi-strategy text fusion over the \texttt {[EOT]}, masked-mean, and masked-attention views), and the two branches are fused adaptively into action-biased prototypes. On the video side, MGTA selects discriminative spatial-temporal regions and performs dual-branch temporal modeling (dense Conv3d + sparse asynchronous attention); a lightweight frame-aggregation mixer (Mixer) then applies a depthwise temporal convolution to the frame features before the temporal mean. Finally, BFEM bidirectionally enhances the video feature and the text prototypes with each other under zero-initialized gates. The CLIP backbone remains frozen throughout.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:overview@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][4][]4}}
